    "content": "# Chapter 9: Database Design and ER Modeling\n\nTeaches students to design databases from business requirements. Covers requirements analysis, the SDLC, entity-relationship modeling, Crow's Foot notation, relationship types, advanced ER concepts, normalization as a design check, ERD-to-table mapping, and common modeling mistakes.\n\n## Chapter Files\n\n- [Main Chapter](ch09-main-2026-06-16.md)\n- [Let's Build](ch09-lets-build-2026-06-16.md)\n- [Review & Reflection](ch09-reflection-2026-06-16.md)\n- [Terms Treasury](ch09-terms-2026-06-16.md)\n- [Readiness Assessment Test](ch09-rat-2026-06-16.md)\n\n## Lab\n\n- [Lab 9 Questions](lab-09-questions-2026-05-22.md)",
